      Subject: fix(storm): slice heavy work and restore beam clusters
      Stat   : 16 files changed, 279 insertions(+), 187 deletions(-)
      Body   : Bound explosion and cluster processing to prevent scheduler task saturation, stabilize mounted head seats and targets, restore reliable beam availability and ground clusters, and harden stale-entity diagnostics.

[617] 339bc3d4f31a6b73208c613e5cf93b0f55c52b93 | 2026-09-04 12:54:31 -0300 | dt=+221s
      Author : Tazo! <[redacted-owner-email]> | Tree: e13dc45351e05e1451050cbe68b7c0697da319c1
      Subject: fix(beam): consume captured mobs at the source
      Stat   : 3 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)
      Body   : Remove non-player entities after they reach the tractor beam origin and avoid touching entity metadata after successful absorption invalidates the handle.

[618] dafd599fb87687bca3eb366cd7b946fe54f74cf9 | 2026-09-04 23:56:49 -0300 | dt=+39738s
      Author : TazoLaTaza <[redacted-owner-email]> | Tree: 7ae4f0717c6e802c18493b3b3d514b010008ed11
      Subject: improved aim from the storm head
      Stat   : 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

[619] 011db05fa0e852bd5169ed1783fea90558696aaa | 2026-09-05 00:34:41 -0300 | dt=+2272s
      Author : Tazo! <[redacted-owner-email]> | Tree: fec06b50490a549eabf948fac62700bf837ce57c
      Subject: Smooth storm heads and constrain cluster absorption to beam paths
      Stat   : 17 files changed, 427 insertions(+), 117 deletions(-)
      Body   : Remove the 2048-task registration cap while preserving scheduler lane budgets and delays. Limit angular speed and acceleration, compensate beam aim offsets, and retain exclusive beam ownership of captured clusters and mobs.
      Body   : 
      Body   : Prioritize visible construction blocks with cached targets and three-ray staggered scans. Fix stairs/bedrock classification and capture the actual construction impact before nearby terrain.
      Body   : 
      Body   : Add 17 controller regression tests, in-game reproduction steps and particle API findings. npm test and npm run build pass against @minecraft/server 2.8.0; Bedrock visual/watchdog validation remains in-game.

[620] c052d20421bb7200d79b3960a55a970018dcbbfc | 2026-09-05 01:13:20 -0300 | dt=+2319s
      Author : Tazo! <[redacted-owner-email]> | Tree: 887e37b9ba873793e7ede790e0cf1e83d6695b7c
      Subject: Fix storm score initialization, absorption speed and construction targeting
      Stat   : 9 files changed, 184 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)
      Body   : Read valid scoreboard identities before evolution flags to avoid missing-identity warnings while preserving score initialization and diagnostics. Double beam travel rates and effective vortex drive/acceleration tuning without changing scheduler cadence or beam ownership.
      Body   : 
      Body   : Raise terrain-relative cruising altitude with seeded smooth low passes and a dimension ceiling margin. Let heads discover single construction blocks even with the beam off, including logs and terracotta, using cached targets and bounded nearby ray/probe sweeps.
      Body   : 
      Body   : Add eight regressions (25 passing total), a geometric construction scene, and manual in-game checks. npm run build passes against @minecraft/server 2.8.0; native physics, visuals and watchdog timing still require in-game validation.

